---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro'
import {
  SITE_URL, COMPANY, CONTACT_EMAIL, ORG_ID, DISCLOSURES_URL, GRIEVANCE_PATH, AMFI_REGISTRATION_URL,
  EDITORIAL_POLICY_PATH, RISK_DISCLAIMER,
} from '../lib/site.js'

const description =
  'Who Nuberry is, what we are registered for, how we are paid by fund houses, the direct plan alternative, and what we do not do.'
// Change this date whenever the disclosures change.
const lastUpdated = '2026-11-06'
const jsonLd = [{
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'WebPage',
  name: 'Disclosures',
  url: `${SITE_URL}${DISCLOSURES_URL}`,
  dateModified: lastUpdated,
  about: { '@id': ORG_ID },
  publisher: { '@id': ORG_ID },
}]
---
<Base
  title="Disclosures: Registration, Commissions and Conflicts | Nuberry"
  description={description}
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
  breadcrumbs={[{ name: 'Disclosures', path: DISCLOSURES_URL }]}
>
  <section class="wrap page-head">
    <span class="eyebrow">How we work</span>
    <h1 class="display">Disclosures</h1>
    <p class="lede">Who we are, what we are registered to do, and how we are paid.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap legal">
    <div class="prose">
      <p><time datetime={lastUpdated}>Last updated 6 November 2026</time></p>

      <h2>Who we are</h2>
      <p>
        Nuberry is a brand of {COMPANY.legalName} (CIN {COMPANY.cin}), registered office {COMPANY.address}. We are a
        mutual fund distributor registered with the Association of Mutual Funds in India (AMFI) under ARN {COMPANY.arn}.
        You can check our registration by searching for ARN {COMPANY.arn} on
        <a href={AMFI_REGISTRATION_URL} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">AMFI's distributor search</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>What we do, and what we don't</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>We help parents open and run mutual fund folios in their child's name, and carry out the transactions they ask for.</li>
        <li>We are a distributor, not a SEBI-registered investment adviser. We don't give personalised investment advice, and nothing on this site is a recommendation to buy any scheme.</li>
        <li>We never hold your money. Payments go from your bank to the fund house, and units are held in your child's name with the fund house and its registrar.</li>
        <li>We don't offer rewards, cashback, gifts or vouchers for investing or for inviting others.</li>
        <li>We don't guarantee returns. {RISK_DISCLAIMER}</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>How we are paid</h2>
      <p>
        Parents pay Nuberry no subscription or account fee. We are paid by fund houses, as a trail commission on the money
        invested through us. Investments made through a distributor go into the <strong>regular plan</strong> of a scheme.
      </p>
      <p>
        Every scheme also has a <strong>direct plan</strong>, which has no distributor commission and so a lower expense
        ratio. The difference in expense ratio is the cost of using a distributor. Over many years it reduces your returns
        compared with the direct plan of the same scheme. You can invest in direct plans yourself, with the fund house or
        through a platform that offers them.
      </p>
      <p>
        Commission rates differ between fund houses and schemes. Before you invest through us, we will tell you the
        commission we receive on the schemes you choose, as AMFI's code of conduct for distributors requires. You can ask
        us for these figures at any time at <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Conflicts of interest</h2>
      <p>
        Because we are paid by fund houses, we could earn more from some schemes than others. We don't rank or pick schemes
        in our guides, we don't accept payment to mention a product, and our calculators work the same for every fund. How
        we write and check our guides is set out in our <a href={EDITORIAL_POLICY_PATH}>editorial policy</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Complaints</h2>
      <p>
        If something has gone wrong, our <a href={GRIEVANCE_PATH}>investor grievance page</a> sets out who to contact, how
        long we take to respond, and how to escalate to the fund house, SEBI SCORES and SMART ODR.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
